What the licence covers
-----------------------

- The KiCad project (ZX-V/ZX-V/: schematic, board, rules, the zxv symbol
  library and the zxv.pretty footprints), the fabrication files (fabrication/:
  Gerber, drill, BOM, CPL and the schematic in PDF) and this folder's README.

Exceptions
----------

- tools/ (the Python scripts that draw the schematic, place, route and make
  the fabrication files): MIT licence, in tools/LICENSE.
- Four footprints in zxv.pretty are modified copies of footprints from the
  KiCad libraries (Jack_3.5mm_PJ-320D_TRS, LED_D3.0mm_Horizontal_O1.27mm_Z2.0mm,
  RaspberryPi_Pico2_Common and SW_SPST_Omron_B3F-315x_Angled). They keep the
  KiCad libraries' licence, CC BY-SA 4.0 with its exception for designs that
  use them: https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/ . Each one says in its
  description where it comes from and what was changed.
- Four footprints in zxv.pretty (BatteryHolder_CR2032-BS-6-1,
  HDMI_A_HC-HDMI0019T-1, SW_Slide_SK12D07VG4_Angled and
  USB_A_904-131A2032S10100) started from the EasyEDA/LCSC component library
  (converted with easyeda2kicad) and were corrected against the
  manufacturers' drawings, as their descriptions say. EasyEDA does not state a
  licence for that library; only the changes made here are licensed under the
  CERN-OHL-W.
- Their 3D models (zxv.3dshapes/*.step) also come from EasyEDA and are not
  published here: the 3D viewer shows those four parts without a body. They
  can be fetched with easyeda2kicad from the LCSC part numbers in the
  footprints ("LCSC Part"). They are not needed to make the board.
- The Raspberry Pi Pico 2 and the other parts are External Material and
  Available Components in the terms of the licence: their own designs are not
  part of this source.

The name
--------

The licence covers the design, not the name. "ZX-V" and its logo are not
licensed: a board made or modified from this source can say that it is based
on the ZX-V board, but it must not be presented as the ZX-V board itself or
as endorsed by the ZX-V project without permission. When You modify the
design, change or remove the name and the version on the silkscreen, and add
the modification notice that section 3.3(b) of the licence asks for.

